{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393828-so-merfolk-houses-are-a-thing","id":1393828,"title":"So Merfolk Houses are a thing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-03T13:03:33-07:00","id":1393828,"title":"So Merfolk Houses are a thing","content":"So in my setting I include Merfolk Houses. And Merfolk are like the Sidhe of their Territory. I\u2019m debating if I should make them have like two major Kingdoms of Like the Empire of Atlantis and the Empire of Avaiki (for the Underworld which the Merfolk Allfather Vaiki live). I\u2019m thinking they view the Pacific maybe as the shallow depths and the deeper depths of Avaiki is the Dreaming proper. Or maybe I would just divide it into a Seven Seas type of separation.<br /> <br /> But in my Headcanon the Merfolk houses have the Merfolk as the Nobles and aquatic Fae like Pooka, Morganed, Selkies, Triton and even some Aquatic Dragonkin join. They also have extended citizenship to some Menehune and coastal Kithain and Oceanic Inanimae. This means Sidhe and Oba could convert to Merfolk Houses.<br /> <br /> With the Merrow I am thinking why not have them have a House Dagon, House Qyrl, and House Murduacha, with some Joining House Balor which has its HQ underwater. Their Nobles are Merrow, Sidhe, and Sevartal and they also have Beasties and unseelie Kithain and Kelpies in their Household.<br /> <br /> The Merfolk Houses got cut for space but the setting is lessened without them. I really feel opening up their territory and Kingdoms does a lot to enrich the game. And they would be in a unique situation since they are all essentially Autumn esque since they reincarnate, but it seems they are written as if they always breed true and have Changeling Children. But we also have Merfolk milk which allows their children to survive the ocean till they become Merfolk. They have entire cities underwater though? So what if we introduced the concept of Kinain to them? So let\u2019s say they are potent enough to always sire Kinain if the children doesn\u2019t become Mer. This makes it more feasible for them to have entire Kingdoms which will be filled with not just Nobles but Kinain, Inanimae, Chimera, and commoner Kiths. Though they would still secretly comprise a huge amount of the Worlds Nobles. And they would have probably a larger percentage of their Changelings Nobles, I still want to make it a little less then Half. That has some interesting dynamics when Nobles aren\u2019t a small portion of the community, it makes things like inequality more noticeable, making more of a privileged class of \u201cSea Founders\u201d.<br /> <br /> Thoughts or do folks not like using Merfolk because they feel they are too distant.<br /> <br /> What about Merfolk Joining the Concordia Houses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T13:19:17-07:00","id":1393837,"title":"","content":"I think Merfolk Houses are a great idea. I think the Merfolk Seamother is female and her name is Vatea, but I\u2019m not 100% sure. Other than that, sounds awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T13:36:22-07:00","id":1393844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393828-so-merfolk-houses-are-a-thing?p=1393837#post1393837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Merfolk Houses are a great idea. I think the Merfolk Seamother is female and her name is Vatea, but I\u2019m not 100% sure. Other than that, sounds awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Merfolk worship the Fish Father of Gods and Mankind Vatea based off the mythology of the island of Mangaia. But they point out the Rokea worship Vatea as Kun the Mother of Fishes.<br /> <br /> It seems to me also a lot of the Merfolk trappings come from Fresh Water Mythic Beings like Syrinx and Lorelei and Apsara forms, which makes me believe the Sundering caused a lot of Fresh Water Fae to take refuge and become reborn as Merfolk.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also love the idea that the Merfolk could have secret islands hidden from Humanity that are essentially homes for their non gilled and amphibious citizens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T14:15:05-07:00","id":1393855,"title":"","content":"Okay<br /> <br /> I like the second paragraph from a cosmology standpoint. The Lorelei were the Sirens of the Rhine River and were much more overtly sexual than the Greek Sirens. Also, Melusine, the Toreador chick who was Mithras\u2019s girlfriend (I think) in V:tDA, is named for a mermaid from the French province of Lusignan.<br /> <br /> The third paragraph is pretty cool too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T15:56:46-07:00","id":1393868,"title":"","content":"Cause of all the supernatural beings Fae would have the easiest time creating and hiding an island risen from<br /> The ocean. For Mages it\u2019s an ordeal that even Archmages would be annoyed by, but Changelings can just do a series of unleashings, and their magic is already geared towards hiding their sacred places. Werewolf\u2019s even imply they learned their special hide Caerns from humans rituals from the Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T02:10:07-07:00","id":1393993,"title":"","content":"Also it feels like the Menehune should have at least one Noble House, same with the Oba who should have multiple Noble Houses, but not as many as the Sidhe. And since the Eshu seemed to have grown to include India as part of their homeland for some reason (my guess is early travels rooted their dream there right before they officially joined with the rest of the Kithain) does that mean the Oba are also there or are they mostly in Africa.<br /> <br /> But the Menehune I feel could have used a different Thallain, like the Paupueo the Owls who hunted the Menehune could have been their natural Thallain. They could have had their own Adhene of the Nawao, kind of like their equivalent of the Firbholg, a people before Menehune and Mankind came to the Islands.<br /> <br /> But I think the Menehune could have shared something like House Lua'nu'u, House Maui, and House Pele (or instead House Laka after the sister of the founder Menehune and daughter of Pele). I could see them sharing Houses with the Maori Fair Folk. As well as some choosing to join one of the Merfolk Houses or House Danu, as House Danu seemed originally to be a Pan Arcadian/Fae Great House and might represent something like a House Pele to them. Similarly Maybe Merfolk have also joined House Danu and to them it represents Vatea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T02:56:33-07:00","id":1394004,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Eshu have India as one of their homelands because their Kinain include the Romani as well as the Yoruba?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T03:03:31-07:00","id":1394006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393828-so-merfolk-houses-are-a-thing?p=1394004#post1394004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the Eshu have India as one of their homelands because their Kinain include the Romani as well as the Yoruba?</div> </div> </div> </div>See I was wondering about that, but that gets confusing because while the Romani originated from India they don't seem particularly culturally tied to there so many centuries afterwards. But that might be the actual reason. Another idea could be some Eshu Converted to Islam and from Islam spread to India and then joined the rest of the Kithain. Like the Satyr's probably started in Greece spread to Italy and North Africa but then spread throughout the West with Hellanism.<br /> <br /> But then they don't seem to really acknowledge the early statements about the Eshu being tied to India very often, except the handful of Eshu that might have a name from the area, they usually tie them to Africa, the Middle East, or just the local Country they are residents of most of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T03:06:12-07:00","id":1394007,"title":"","content":"The Islam idea works too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T12:05:47-07:00","id":1394107,"title":"","content":"This made me remember how house balor thinks selkies are some distant cousins and of nobility too. (Well, selkies in fact even had a queen)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T12:32:04-07:00","id":1394115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rucun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393828-so-merfolk-houses-are-a-thing?p=1394107#post1394107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This made me remember how house balor thinks selkies are some distant cousins and of nobility too. (Well, selkies in fact even had a queen)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it was a hoot that house Balor recognizes it the most due to their descent from Balor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T17:21:56-07:00","id":1394189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393828-so-merfolk-houses-are-a-thing?p=1394115#post1394115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah it was a hoot that house Balor recognizes it the most due to their descent from Balor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I particularly liked the part about Merfolk and Selkies could gain Title in House Balor. Just straight up, swear the Oath, do the Fraility, congrats you are a Noble now, same rights as a Sidhe. Which is a big deal in such a racist House (commoners weren't allowed to get too many dots), though not sure if that is still a thing in C20<br /> Combined with the fact that the Freehold that holds their (current) High Lord is underwater and in middle of the ocean (beyond the 9th wave), I like to imagine that Mer and Selkie Balorians were looking after it while the rest of the House was in Arcadia. The the Resurgence happened and the Arcadians attacked them because they didn't recognise them or they didn't care.<br /> <br /> Yeah, my version of House Balor is a lot more involved in the oceans in WoD, just because they kept their best stuff there. )And they have lots of family there. And it let them mess with anyone travelling over the oceans.) Also on the verge of multiple coups, because a High Lord raised by BSDs is an awful idea and someone would notice that.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, multiple Mer Kingdoms sounds legit. Lots of space under the sea. I would stress that Atlantis and the like are probably in the Dreaming proper, but having a Kingdom co-opt the name because they found/own a Trod that let's them go there quickly is kind of awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T20:08:56-07:00","id":1394222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393828-so-merfolk-houses-are-a-thing?p=1394189#post1394189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I particularly liked the part about Merfolk and Selkies could gain Title in House Balor. Just straight up, swear the Oath, do the Fraility, congrats you are a Noble now, same rights as a Sidhe. Which is a big deal in such a racist House (commoners weren't allowed to get too many dots), though not sure if that is still a thing in C20<br /> Combined with the fact that the Freehold that holds their (current) High Lord is underwater and in middle of the ocean (beyond the 9th wave), I like to imagine that Mer and Selkie Balorians were looking after it while the rest of the House was in Arcadia. The the Resurgence happened and the Arcadians attacked them because they didn't recognise them or they didn't care.<br /> <br /> Yeah, my version of House Balor is a lot more involved in the oceans in WoD, just because they kept their best stuff there. )And they have lots of family there. And it let them mess with anyone travelling over the oceans.) Also on the verge of multiple coups, because a High Lord raised by BSDs is an awful idea and someone would notice that.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, multiple Mer Kingdoms sounds legit. Lots of space under the sea. I would stress that Atlantis and the like are probably in the Dreaming proper, but having a Kingdom co-opt the name because they found/own a Trod that let's them go there quickly is kind of awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that's an idea Atlantis as their equivalent of Arcadia. Or maybe have Atlantis on Earth and their Dreaming Home as Mu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T12:07:54-07:00","id":1394403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393828-so-merfolk-houses-are-a-thing?p=1394189#post1394189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I particularly liked the part about Merfolk and Selkies could gain Title in House Balor. Just straight up, swear the Oath, do the Fraility, congrats you are a Noble now, same rights as a Sidhe. Which is a big deal in such a racist House (commoners weren't allowed to get too many dots), though not sure if that is still a thing in C20<br /> Combined with the fact that the Freehold that holds their (current) High Lord is underwater and in middle of the ocean (beyond the 9th wave), I like to imagine that Mer and Selkie Balorians were looking after it while the rest of the House was in Arcadia. The the Resurgence happened and the Arcadians attacked them because they didn't recognise them or they didn't care.<br /> <br /> Yeah, my version of House Balor is a lot more involved in the oceans in WoD, just because they kept their best stuff there. )And they have lots of family there. And it let them mess with anyone travelling over the oceans.) Also on the verge of multiple coups, because a High Lord raised by BSDs is an awful idea and someone would notice that.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, multiple Mer Kingdoms sounds legit. Lots of space under the sea. I would stress that Atlantis and the like are probably in the Dreaming proper, but having a Kingdom co-opt the name because they found/own a Trod that let's them go there quickly is kind of awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I might be Wrong, but The High-lord Li-Tili is a kinda considered a rogue agent in his own house right now isn't it? His freehold is not a hub of power where every balor enters, but more akin to secluded place where he is hiding alone and avoiding contact with the rest of the house. Many balor fear he is bedlam and not sound of mind anymore. At least I've read it somewhere.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I did a chronicle where they went to his underwater fortress to slay him, and there were several sekies and merfolk servants and nobles protecting him on top of the black spiral dancers. In fact, I considered that the freehold itself was not dry, but magixally flooded, so all battle had to take place underwater, selkies, merfolks and werewolfs had great advantages, meanwhile swinging a sword or trying to fire a pistol was almost impossible.<br /> <br /> (BTW, players were not the main elite force doing the killing, but rather scouts to a group of legendary changelings, including Lady Sierra, and a homebrew queen of lancaster) <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T17:34:27-07:00","id":1394671,"title":"","content":"I've always thought there was a missed opportunity by not leaning into religious titles with the merfolk after all Seabishops are a mythological thing. I am not really sure how i'd make it work though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T18:20:20-07:00","id":1394684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393828-so-merfolk-houses-are-a-thing?p=1394671#post1394671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always thought there was a missed opportunity by not leaning into religious titles with the merfolk after all Seabishops are a mythological thing. I am not really sure how i'd make it work though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but then they would have to wear funny Hats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T19:26:54-07:00","id":1394697,"title":"","content":"I would point out that of the official Merfolk Houses, only one is seen as 'Noble'. The Mer Houses are more like castes, right down to required Apsara and physical traits. Syrinx as leader/nobility, Melusine as scholars/surface diplomats and Lorelei as Warrior/soldier/predators.<br /> I believe that Blood Dimmed Tides had every Merfolk as members of a House.<br /> <br /> That said, I have mentioned that I deviate from that position. But it might provide some ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T08:26:25-07:00","id":1394775,"title":"","content":"I forgot. Melusine was a Merfolk House too. Named for the mermaid who married Raymond of Lusignan and had two kids with him (Sibylla and Guy?) until she left after he walked in on her bathing despite her explicitly telling him never to disturb her during her alone time in her pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T15:52:51-07:00","id":1394863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393828-so-merfolk-houses-are-a-thing?p=1394684#post1394684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah but then they would have to wear funny Hats.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And? A crown is just a funny hat too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T18:49:53-07:00","id":1394928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393828-so-merfolk-houses-are-a-thing?p=1394863#post1394863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And? A crown is just a funny hat too.</div> </div> </div> </div>So they should where crowns. It creates less drag than the hats bishop's wear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T20:38:05-07:00","id":1394974,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1624_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1624\" data-vbnamecard=\"1624\">FallenEco</a> they\u2019re called miters. But yeah, crowns look cooler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T00:33:32-07:00","id":1395026,"title":"","content":"To be Fair I think Miters would be cool to incorporate into the Merrow, like a Priest position. I always liked stories that interpreted Seabishops as more creepy undersea horror.<br /> <br /> Or hell I can see a separate Seabishop Kith as the Priests of the Sea.<br /> <br /> But I think Syrinx as the Leaders/High Nobles is more like how Gwydion view themselves as the Noblest of the Nobles rather then the exclusive nobility. The Mer are described as seeing themselves as all Being Noble.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T01:36:02-07:00","id":1395037,"title":"","content":"Noted. Miters made out of coral would be cool.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I can see the Merfolk classifing themselves as all noble the way the Sidhe do. I would not like a Seabishop kith, but a society or even a House (as a religious group) would be interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T02:39:31-07:00","id":1395041,"title":"","content":"Seabishops are described as Bygones in The Bygone Bestiary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T03:00:43-07:00","id":1395045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393828-so-merfolk-houses-are-a-thing?p=1395041#post1395041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seabishops are described as Bygones in The Bygone Bestiary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely forgot about that book! I forgot how its a super useful sourcebook for making Chimeras for use in Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T03:46:32-07:00","id":1395291,"title":"","content":"Bygones likely also have lookalike counterparts in the Dreaming.<br /> 'Planes' that are reflection of human thoughts and feelings include more than a few redundancy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T04:31:55-07:00","id":1395296,"title":"","content":"Do Bygones live in the Dreaming? I know most of them left Earth after the Sundering ended the Heroic Age of Greek mythology. Or do they have like their own separate realms in the High Umbra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T05:02:12-07:00","id":1395305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393828-so-merfolk-houses-are-a-thing?p=1395296#post1395296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Bygones live in the Dreaming? I know most of them left Earth after the Sundering ended the Heroic Age of Greek mythology. Or do they have like their own separate realms in the High Umbra?</div> </div> </div> </div>Officially, I think it is a case by case basis. Bygones are supposed to be weird remnants, leftover odds and ends that don't really fit anywhere.<br /> And the difference between certain realms of the Far/Deep Dreaming and the High Umbra is...more a matter of how one gets there than a meaningful difference. It is not even a merely academic one in some cases. Which goes a long way to explain the differences inherent to the Nunnehi and the Hsien now that I think about it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T05:14:40-07:00","id":1395309,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1624_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1624\" data-vbnamecard=\"1624\">FallenEco</a> cool. I wonder if Arcadia and Tir Nan Og (the realm of the Celtic pantheon in the High Umbra) could be the same place. Or at least related.<br /> <br /> The Nunnehi and the Hsien are tied to the Umbra rather than the Dreaming, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T08:36:30-07:00","id":1395355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393828-so-merfolk-houses-are-a-thing?p=1395309#post1395309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> cool. I wonder if Arcadia and Tir Nan Og (the realm of the Celtic pantheon in the High Umbra) could be the same place. Or at least related.<br /> <br /> The Nunnehi and the Hsien are tied to the Umbra rather than the Dreaming, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hsien are tied to the Heavens of the Middle Kingdom and are in Exile until they transcend it through enlightenment to get the Jade key which unlocks their ability to enter the Umbra but they still are barred from the Paradise of the August Personage of Jades Heavenly Palace.<br /> My personal theory is they were Fae who were tamed to Obey the Gods so long ago in the Past, while in the rest of the World the Tuatha has their Fae children essentially run amok doing whatever they want as their own Gods. Back then they didn\u2019t know of the Dreaming as the Dreaming but only as the Mists.<br /> <br /> And the Nunnehi were tied to the dreaming and the umbra, and when their version of Arcadia was cut off for them they compensated with their affinity with the Umbra. In C20 they go to both the Umbra and the Dreaming, originally I believe they only had access to the Umbra in older editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T08:39:15-07:00","id":1395356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393828-so-merfolk-houses-are-a-thing?p=1395305#post1395305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Officially, I think it is a case by case basis. Bygones are supposed to be weird remnants, leftover odds and ends that don't really fit anywhere.<br /> And the difference between certain realms of the Far/Deep Dreaming and the High Umbra is...more a matter of how one gets there than a meaningful difference. It is not even a merely academic one in some cases. Which goes a long way to explain the differences inherent to the Nunnehi and the Hsien now that I think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I Agree! It has long been my belief that the Deep Umbra and Deep Dreaming where essentially two sides of the same coin and it colored your interaction with it depending on how you got there. It\u2019s the deepest layer of reality, and while this version of the WoD doesn\u2019t have the Supernal Realms this is close to the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T09:18:14-07:00","id":1395364,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1624_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1624\" data-vbnamecard=\"1624\">FallenEco</a> I like your theory. Is the Yang World referred to in Land of Eight Million Dreams the Middle Umbra, the High Umbra, both or neither? Or are the three layers of the Umbra basically irrelevant to the Changeling cosmology?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T09:19:19-07:00","id":1395365,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> I like that! That totally makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T14:01:52-07:00","id":1395456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393828-so-merfolk-houses-are-a-thing?p=1395364#post1395364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1624_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1624\" data-vbnamecard=\"1624\">FallenEco</a> I like your theory. Is the Yang World referred to in Land of Eight Million Dreams the Middle Umbra, the High Umbra, both or neither? Or are the three layers of the Umbra basically irrelevant to the Changeling cosmology?</div> </div> </div> </div>The layers of the Umbra can basically correspond to the layers of of the Dreaming. WoD has...issues with their eastern cosmology and it's semi-incompatibility. My understanding is that yes, some parts of the Umbra are noted as Yang Worlds. So are some parts of the Dreaming. Other parts of the Dreaming correspond to Ying Worlds, just like the Underworkd. In short, both?<br /> Which is another three layer (Shadowlands, Tempest, Labyrinth) otherworld, albeit one that is more born from memory than thought but it does fit the pattern.<br /> And generally, the Umbra should be irrelevant to Changeling games in general, unless one is playing Gallain with ties to one, or gets off at the wrong point of a trod. Kithain don't really have ways to get there or navigate back in their toolkit.<br /> <br /> As for Arcadia and Tir Nan Og, they are likely to be extremely similar and close (like only natives can tell the difference) if they aren't same. And I mean close literally, both the Deep Umbra and the Dreaming are conceptual spaces, with 'geography' being more about ideas and associations.<br /> I would argue that the closer to the mundane world, the easier it becomes to distinguish between the Dreaming and the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Anyway...Merfolk Houses, should we add more? The current three represent the dominant religion and their society anyway. House Balor could try to recruit any not already in a House, (just like selkies), so there is president. Plus Banner Houses are a thing. If we dip into extended material, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/299635/Kiths-of-Arcadia?src=also_purchased\" target=\"_blank\">tritons</a> are a thing so other sea-going kiths aren't outside the realms of possibility. Plus any Gallain. What is the relationship between the Mer and the Ondines, as an example?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 06-09-2020, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}